ription paths\nQ14 adjudication source/answer matched 24 distinct description paths\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"**The registered STOP stands. Both range controls passed their range check, and both adjudicators agreed that Q10’s $108 billion midpoint was valid. Ask Alex to authorize one more blinded read with the full instructions the writers saw.**\n\n1. **Serious — Q10 was scored correctly.** Both first readers marked the same figure as misread. Under the registered rule, that alone stops the run. Both adjudicators cleared the mark because the writer quoted “$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%” in full and used the permitted midpoint. The two range controls also behaved as intended. Both readers flagged the $36–43 billion range when it was placed in the disjoint $20–30 billion band. Neither flagged the overlapping band or Q07’s range. Across the 12 original replies, the re-read left 12 of 14 forecasts supported and two split. Every case still had a usable reply, and both joint replies supported both forecasts. [Registered rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:244) · [Q10 adjudication](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread-adjudication/Q10.md:29) · [Re-read tally](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/REREAD-TALLY.json:190)\n\n2. **Minor — The overlap control passed a narrower test than the report’s wording suggests.** The builder added the new $36–43 billion forecast but kept the old 85% growth assumption and $37 billion forecast in the explanation. Both readers correctly flagged the competing figures. That leaves the range result intact, though “must not be marked” is broad enough to suggest a clean answer was expected. The disjoint control also retained prose naming the correct band, giving readers a second clue. Clean both explanations and render the controls like the original replies. Also fix the control adjudication path before relying on it. If readers split, the builder would look for an original writer file named `C-overlap.json` or `C-disjoint.json`. Neither control split on its range mark this time. [Control registration](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:306) · [Control builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread.py:23) · [Overlap reading](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread-packets/Q12.codex.json:14) · [Adjudication builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_adjudicate.py:84)\n\n3. **Serious — Give readers the same rule text as adjudicators.** Use one shared source for the writer’s system text, all schema descriptions, and the definitions readers apply. The current readers got the passages and answer. The adjudicators also got the writer’s rules, which resolved both the midpoint mark and Q10’s separate rounding mark. I counted **11 midpoint marks** across the four readings, in groups of 4, 3, 2, and 2. Both adjudicators rejected every one. The risk runs the other way too. A format permission can make readers overlook a wrong value or give too much credit to a weak assumption. Have readers check the quote and the calculation against the format, and separately say which evidence supports the assumption that puts the forecast in its chosen band. [Reader packet builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_reread.py:63) · [Adjudication rules and writer instructions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread-adjudication/Q10.md:24) · [Q10 rounding decision](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread-adjudication/Q10.codex.json:16)\n\n4. **Serious — The spending forecast still shows how much the result can depend on who reads it.** The first adjudicators rejected the 90% share as unsupported. Both fresh readers accepted the identical reply. At $745 billion of total spending, 90% gives $670.5 billion, while about 94% reaches $700 billion and changes the band. The cited Meta figure covers one company, and the Zacks passage offers only “a large portion” for AI infrastructure. The other spending reply, Q07, stayed split even with the full format rules in adjudication. Its reference also still measures total spending. A second re-read can test whether readers apply the format consistently. A fresh vote on these same replies gives limited evidence about whether the spending forecast is reliable. [First ruling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/adjudication/R07.codex.json:3) · [Fresh reading](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread-packets/Q08.claude.json:1) · [Q07 adjudication](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind3-2026-11-22/reread-adjudication/Q07.codex.json:3) · [Council 57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r57.md:7)\n\n**Recommendation.** Take the STOP and the spending disagreement to Alex now. Ask him to authorize one bounded, blinded re-read of the same 12 replies, with the shared instructions and controls agreed before release. A fourth writer run would change the answers while the open question is how readers judge them. D743 authorized the range repair and one re-read. [Alex’s authorization](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11434)\n\n**Falsifier.** The revised reading must accept the full quote recorded as $108 billion and catch the identical quote recorded as $108.5 billion. I checked that changing only that value triggers the number check. It must also distinguish clean overlapping and disjoint bands, and flag a format-correct forecast whose decisive assumption lacks support. A failed control or any registered stop ends the re-read. Report both spending replies’ support votes and reasons alongside the verdict. [Source-number check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:477) · [Registered scoring](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:319)"}}
